Miciri @VERSION@ (Windows x64, VST3)

WHAT WAS INSTALLED
  Plug-in      Miciri.vst3 in the standard VST3 folder
               (normally C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3).
  This folder  License texts, third-party notices, this file and the uninstaller.
  Nothing else: no background service, no automatic update, no telemetry.
  Audio is analysed in memory only. It is never written to disk or sent anywhere,
  and the plug-in passes it through bit for bit.

UNINSTALL
  Windows Settings > Apps > Miciri, or run unins000.exe in this folder.

WEBVIEW2 RUNTIME
  The plug-in window is drawn with the Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime, which is
  part of current Windows 10 and 11. The runtime is not bundled with this
  installer. If it is missing, the plug-in shows a fallback panel instead of its
  usual window; install the Evergreen runtime from Microsoft to get the full window.

LICENSE
  Miciri is free software under GPL-3.0-or-later (see LICENSE). This binary
  combines Miciri with JUCE (used under AGPL-3.0), the VST3 SDK (GPL-3.0),
  pocketfft (BSD-3-Clause) and the Microsoft WebView2 loader (BSD-3-Clause,
  binary). The combined binary is distributed under GPLv3 and the JUCE parts under
  AGPLv3. The texts are in LICENSES\, and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md lists the
  third-party components.

CORRESPONDING SOURCE (GPLv3 section 6(d))
  Miciri @VERSION@   https://github.com/synchain-oss/miciri
                     commit @COMMIT@
  JUCE @JUCE_VERSION@          https://github.com/juce-framework/JUCE
                     commit @JUCE_COMMIT@
  Microsoft.Web.WebView2 @WEBVIEW2_VERSION@ (NuGet package; the loader is linked
                     statically as a binary, so its source is not part of the
                     corresponding source)

  To rebuild: check out the two commits above, then
    cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DJUCE_PATH=<JUCE checkout> -DMICIRI_HOST_PROBE=OFF
    cmake --build build
  The VST3 bundle is then under build\src\plugin.
